      "writtenOn": "2023-01-16T07:24:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s because you didn\u0027t wait for LinkProperties, I think. You should :\n• wifiCallback.expectAvailableCallbacksDoubleValidated (or some variant of expectAvailableCallbacks*)\n• THEN wifiCallback.expect(LINK_PROPERTIES_CHANGED, mWifiNetworkAgent)\n\nThe problem here is that if you only expect AVAILABLE, you\u0027re unblocking immediately after the `connect` event has gone through, but not for link properties. If you said `eventuallyExpect(LINK_PROPERTIES_CHANGED...`, then you matched the first one, so you also unblock before the change is effective.",
